permalink: /robots.txt
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
layout: false
---
{#- Written as a template rather than kept in a static folder so the sitemap
    line follows `url` in site_settings.json. A robots.txt that names a sitemap
    on the wrong domain is worse than none: it is the one file a crawler reads
    first, and it would point every one of them somewhere else.

    Nothing is disallowed. The build report is the only page that does not want
    indexing and it carries its own `noindex` meta; naming it here as well would
    be wrong the moment an author publishes a page of their own at that URL,
    which writeStatusPage() deliberately allows. -#}
User-agent: *
Allow: /

Sitemap: {{ '/sitemap.xml' | absolute }}
